<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antioch</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antioch was an ancient city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-river">Orontes River</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus I</a>, it became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> and later one of the great cities of the Roman East. It was captured more than once by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, notably in 540.</p></div>
